<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Movilla Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 540</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Movilla Abbey was a monastery at Newtownards in County Down, Northern Ireland, founded around 540 by Saint Finnian of Movilla. It became one of the leading monastic schools of early medieval Ulster and is said to have taught Saint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columba">Columba</a>. It later became an Augustinian priory, dissolved in the 16th century; ruins of its church survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/movilla-abbey.jpg" alt="Movilla Abbey" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dennis Reynolds · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Movilla_Abbey,_Newtownards_-_geograph.org.uk_-_84296.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
